==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|spook|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/spuːki/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spooky.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːki|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[eerie|Eerie]], or suggestive of [[ghost]]s or the [[supernatural]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} Spooked; [[afraid]]; [[frightened]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Wilbur Page|title=I Had to Do It My Way!: One Man's Journey Through Life|page=88
|passage=I thought it was nice, though I found it very quiet, and whenever I was alone in it, I felt '''spooky'''.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[unpredictably|Unpredictably]] [[excitable]]; [[skittish]] (used especially of horses).

